ithub.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108795.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #42630\r\n\r\nThis PR adds an informational message when the Dummy audio driver is explicitly selected by the user, making it easier to diagnose audio configuration issues.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- Print `\"No audio (using dummy audio driver)\"` when Dummy\r\ndriver is explicitly chosen\r\n- Message appears only when:\r\n  - Dummy is selected via `--audio-driver Dummy` command line\r\nargument\r\n  - Dummy is set in project settings\r\n(`audio/driver/driver=\"Dummy\"`)\r\n  - Running in editor mode (not in exported projects)\r\n  - Not in headless mode\r\n- Existing warning for fallback scenario remains unchanged\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\nTested on Linux with the following scenarios:\r\n- [x] `--audio-driver Dummy` - message appears\r\n- [x] Project settings with `driver/driver=\"Dummy\"` - message\r\nappears\r\n- [x] `--headless` mode - no message (as expected)\r\n- [x] Explicit selection of other drivers (PulseAudio) - no\r\nmessage\r\n- [x] Fallback to Dummy preserves existing warning behavior","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108795/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108795/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}